1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Dohna_nr_65#TAB4 '''Carl Christoffer Delphicus Dohna'''], född 1748-09-30 på Hjulsta, död 1752-11-06 på Stjärnsund och begraven i Askersunds kyrka .
2 CONT
2 CONT Interesting Ghost Story:
2 CONT
2 CONT Tidö castle is situated southwest of Västerås in Västmanland, Sweden. Axel Oxenstierna who was Gustav II Adolf’s Chancellor and also Queen Christinas guardian took the help of architects Simon de la Vallee and Nicodemus Tessin sen
2 CONC ior to build the castle in 1620 - 1642.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the eighteenth century there was a little boy who lived there. His name was Karl Kristoffer Deficius Dohna and he was the son of count Fritz Karl Dohna and Fredrika Ulrika Sture. According to legend he had been told to stay awa
2 CONC y from the various old tunnels underneath the castle, but being a curious child he did not listen but sneaked away and took off into a tunnel to explore. Soon he was lost and could’t find his way out. The boy was never found again
2 CONC  but died a gruesome death in the cold, damp and rat filled tunnels underground.
2 CONT
2 CONT You can still hear his ghost screaming for help at night looking for a way out, a scared, lonely tormented sound. 
