1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT === Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/index.php?title=Ridderstolpe-3&errcode=saved
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Carl von Frischen Ridderstolpe, Count.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born September 24, 1864, in Stockholm, the son of Carl Gustaf Ridderstolpe and Augusta Liljencrantz.
2 CONT
2 CONT Student at the Naval Academy September 30, 1879. Naval officer's examination October 6, 1887. Second lieutenant in the naval reserve on October 28 of the same year.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lay judge in Snävringe district of Västmanland County in 1893. Managing director of Mälsåkers Aktiebolag in 1896.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lieutenant in the naval reserve on March 18, 1898.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died on July 27, 1905, in Solna parish, Stockholm County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Owned part of Barkarö in Likanämnd parish and Lövsta in Dingtuna parish, Västmanland County, from 1891 to 1895, as well as Hov in Svinngarn parish, Uppsala County, from 1891 to 1895.
2 CONT
2 CONT Leased Giresta in Rytterne parish, Västmanland County, from 1889 to 1896. Owned Årsta in Sköldinge parish, Södermanland County, from December 1, 1896, and held the entailed estates of Fiholm and Giresta after his father's death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married on August 28, 1894, in Getå to Ingeborg Sofia Nobel, born on April 25, 1865, in Helsinki, died on May 11, 1939, in Oscars förs, Stockholm, daughter of engineer Robert Hjalmar Nobel and Paulina Sofia Carolina Lenngrén.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT Carl von Frischen Ridderstolpe, greve. https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Ridderstolpe_nr_119#TAB_6
2 CONT Född 1864-09-24 i Stockholm.
2 CONT Död 1905-07-27 i Solna socken, Stockholms län.
2 CONT Gift 1894-08-28 Getå med Ingeborg Sofia Nobel, född 1865-04-25 i Helsingfors, död 1939-05-11 i Oscars förs, Stockholm, dotter av ingenjören Robert Hjalmar Nobel och Paulina Sofia Carolina Lenngrén
