1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Catharina Leijel''' (Lyell?) (née Allestrec) married to [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Leijel_nr_1531#TAB_6 '''Henrik Leijel'''] from Sweden. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I wonder if the surname '''Allestrec''' is correct? 
2 CONT
2 CONT Geni doesn't know a single individual with that surname. I'd argue it's a surname that sounds or looks like that. Something onomatopoetic to it. That's very typical in Swedish records. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Alister''? ''Alistair''? Someting of the sort. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Lyell'', too? Then the name [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Leijel_nr_1531#TAB_1 '''Leijel'''], originally Lyell, was changed back. Adelsvapen claims, though, that the name was [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Leijel_
2 CONC nr_1531#TAB_2 Leijel] in Scotland in 1612, "Aberbrothock i Skottland".   
2 CONT
2 CONT Another case in point: Please see the daughter. Married to: 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Richard West, 4th Earl '''De La Warr''', in Adelsvapen "'''Delawarr'''". 
